# Cursor working rules — Agentic Trading

`AGENTS.md` (the same file as `CLAUDE.md` via symlink) is the canonical source of truth; read
it in full before non-trivial work. This file only points Cursor at the must-dos so they are
not missed.

## Read first
`AGENTS.md` → `STATUS.md` → `PLAN.md` → relevant `docs/phase-*.md` → latest `docs/rollouts/*`
→ `git log -3` + current diff.

## Your role: the human review cockpit
Cursor is the human-in-the-loop seat in the `main` integration worktree (`~/Code/Agentic
Trading`) — review, steer, hand-edit, resolve merge conflicts, and integrate the `agent/*`
branches. You are NOT a fourth autonomous agent. If you run Cursor's agent/background mode on a
feature, keep it on its own `cursor/*` branch and merge it like any `agent/*` branch; never turn
`main` into an autonomous lane.

## Pre-commit / handoff protocol (MANDATORY before any commit or push)
1. `STATUS.md` — current state, blockers, next action.
2. `docs/rollouts/YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.md` — new or updated note: summary, why, exact files
   touched, verification commands actually run, follow-ups. (Do not use a single `HANDOFF.md`.)
3. `PLAN.md` — reflect any scope / timeline / approach change.
4. Relevant phase doc(s) under `docs/`.
5. Reference which docs you updated in the commit message.

## Verify before claiming done — in this order
- `npx tsc --noEmit`   (type errors — fast, do this first)
- `npm test`           (vitest)
- `npm run build`      (full Next.js build; also re-checks types)

`npm run build` wipes and regenerates `.next/`; restart any running dev server afterward.

## Hard guardrails
- Real trading app, owner accepts 100% risk (see AGENTS.md "Product philosophy — real trading,
  owner's risk"). There is NO Test-mode/local-sim and NO `paperMode` default — an account is an
  account (a broker paper account is just a connected account by `environment`). Test against a
  connected broker account; keep the existing typed-confirm ritual before toggling an account live.
  Do NOT re-add paper-as-default or "protect the owner's money from your bugs" paternalism — harden
  CORRECTNESS + multi-user safety, not obedience.
- No destructive git (`reset --hard`, force-push, branch deletion) without explicit
  confirmation in the current conversation.
- Edit only your own worktree; do not edit another tool's `agent/*` worktree.
- Never label real data "mock" / "fallback" in anything user-facing (see AGENTS.md).
